{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1499363-should-the-long-flight-be-using-western-element-manipulation","id":1499363,"title":"Should the Long Flight be Using Western Element Manipulation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-11T05:36:37-08:00","id":1499363,"title":"Should the Long Flight be Using Western Element Manipulation","content":"So, I am interested in opinions on whether the Long Flight for the most part should be using the Western Elements for Elemental Manipulation or not. Ryu and Long (Japanese and Chinese Dragons) in my opinion would more likely be using the Wuxing (or Five Agents- Wood, Water, Metal, Earth, and Fire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T07:27:39-08:00","id":1499368,"title":"","content":"My layman's understanding (and if anyone knows better, please correct me) is that the Chinese concept of Wuxing (translating as &quot;five phases&quot; or &quot;five agents&quot;) - fire, water, wood, metal, earth - are conceived as metaphysical agents of change to describe the interrelationship and interaction between phenomenon. (This apparently includes everything from fortune telling and traditional medicine to music and military strategy.) It's not really supposed to correspond with the four Hellenic &quot;classical elements&quot; or fire, air, earth and water. <br /> <br /> And again, I'm not an expert, but I believe you have a similar thing with the Indian/Buddhist concept of Mah\u0101bh\u016bta (&quot;great element&quot;) of earth, water, fire, air, ether/void, where they are cosmic principles rather than actual physical elements. <br /> <br /> Japan apparently has both concepts, Gogyo for Wuxing and Godai for Mah\u0101bh\u016bta. <br /> <br /> Then there's the Hindu concept of Pancha Bhoota, which may be more in line with the classical elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T05:58:10-08:00","id":1499512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1499363-should-the-long-flight-be-using-western-element-manipulation#post1499363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I am interested in opinions on whether the Long Flight for the most part should be using the Western Elements for Elemental Manipulation or not. Ryu and Long (Japanese and Chinese Dragons) in my opinion would more likely be using the Wuxing (or Five Agents- Wood, Water, Metal, Earth, and Fire).</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be nice, still... I see no reason, why it should be more needed for eastern dragons, than scions. Still probably most useful it would be for eastern sorcerers and more as a principle, than that they can command one particular element.<br /> <br /> Btw, I think I never heard about mythological mention of eastern dragon having a particular power over metal or wood... Ok, some growt, fertility magic would probably work good for them (which would fall into wood element stuff), but... ability to manipulate metal seems quite of to me. I never heard and when I try to think about, animal representing metal is white tiger and if I am not mistaking a least China see quite antagonism/rivalry between dragons and tigers.<br /> <br /> It's just, when I thinking about eastern dragons, it's I just think, that system is missing some possibility of leaning more into physical/magical prowess (as you have set number of spells based on inheritance). As I couldn't avoid a feel, that eastern dragons tend to lean more to magic than western. Like... they fly, but not because of wings, but because of magic and their mythology... Well, without a dragon book, I would see absolutely no problems, to say, than eastern dragons are just subtype of gods (or titans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25570-ilicius","name":"Ilicius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T15:07:37-08:00","id":1499580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilicius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1499363-should-the-long-flight-be-using-western-element-manipulation?p=1499512#post1499512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Btw, I think I never heard about mythological mention of eastern dragon having a particular power over metal or wood... Ok, some growt, fertility magic would probably work good for them (which would fall into wood element stuff), but... ability to manipulate metal seems quite of to me. I never heard and when I try to think about, animal representing metal is white tiger and if I am not mistaking a least China see quite antagonism/rivalry between dragons and tigers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the really old Daoist material still lying around depict five dragons, each for the Five Agents/Vectors/etc, instead of the more familiar Four Spirits + the Yellow Dragon schema. Or just two dragons, each for East and West.<br /> <br /> In any case, the spirits/gods/beasts/dragons \u2018having power over\u2019 the Wu Xing is sorta like\u2026 the Ouroboros \u2018having power over\u2019 infinity or alchemy. That is, they were originally meant to be symbols (or totems?), not \u2018real gods\u2019 like Zeus or Odin who explicitly wield awesome supernatural power. But modern depictions go for the Rule Of Cool, hence the elemental-kinesis powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T12:31:44-08:00","id":1503961,"title":"","content":"Well, I think it's more complicated also because are a few East Asian Philosophies that refer to elements, but use sometimes the same differently. Like, in Daoism, Earth simbolyzes harmony, sustaining and, in general, the idea of some kind of help. In Book of the Five Rings, inspired by Zen Buddhism, the concept of Earth is related to resistance and endurance, &quot;be unmovable like the mountain&quot; and such. So... It really sounds editorially hard to make all of this fit in a single book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}